{"tool_name":"chopper","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"chopper","home":"https://github.com/wdecoster/chopper","license":"MIT","summary":"Rust implementation of NanoFilt+NanoLyse, both originally written in Python. This tool, intended for long read sequencing such as PacBio or ONT, filters and trims a fastq file.","addition_date":"2025-06-18T09:20:19.874306Z","last_update_date":"2025-06-30T15:46:01.095401Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["v0.10.0b"],"collections":["ONTeater"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:chopper","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"decosterwouter@gmail.com","name":"Wouter de Coster","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5248-8197","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"],"url":"https://gigabaseorgigabyte.wordpress.com"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"cmd":"gunzip -c reads.fastq.gz | chopper -q 10 -l 500 | gzip > filtered_reads.fastq.gz\nchopper -q 10 -l 500 -i reads.fastq > filtered_reads.fastq\nchopper -q 10 -l 500 -i reads.fastq.gz | gzip > filtered_reads.fastq.gz","input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (nucleic acid)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1234"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Data filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (nucleic acid)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1234"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence set (nucleic acid)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1234"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Box-Whisker plot plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2943"},{"term":"Scatter plot plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2940"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"JPG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3579"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Chopper","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Keiler_Collier","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btad311","metadata":{"abstract":"Increases in the cohort size in long-read sequencing projects necessitate more efficient software for quality assessment and processing of sequencing data from Oxford Nanopore Technologies and Pacific Biosciences. Here, we describe novel tools for summarizing experiments, filtering datasets, visualizing phased alignments results, and updates to the NanoPack software suite. Availability and implementation: The cramino, chopper, kyber, and phasius tools are written in Rust and available as executable binaries without requiring installation or managing dependencies. Binaries build on musl are available for broad compatibility. NanoPlot and NanoComp are written in Python3. Links to the separate tools and their documentation can be found at https://github.com/wdecoster/nanopack. All tools are compatible with Linux, Mac OS, and the MS Windows Subsystem for Linux and are released under the MIT license. The repositories include test data, and the tools are continuously tested using GitHub Actions and can be installed with the conda dependency manager.","authors":[{"name":"De Coster W."},{"name":"Rademakers R."}],"citationCount":211,"date":"2023-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"NanoPack2: population-scale evaluation of long-read sequencing data"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Chopper","home":"https://bio.tools/chopper","license":"MIT","version":"v0.10.0b","summary":"Rust implementation of NanoFilt+NanoLyse, both originally written in Python. This tool, intended for long read sequencing such as PacBi